  <diagram name="SD3 Dispute" id="sd3">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1036" dy="529" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2280" pageHeight="2344" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="sd3-53" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" value="SD3 – Dispute: raise (B12), escalate with evidence trail (D6), moderator resolves (I4), or withdrawal" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="26" width="1500" x="20" y="10" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sd3-54" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#f8f8f8;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=11;spacing=8;" value="Version 1.1 draft  |  Date 2026-10-11  |  Author: Student 3  |  Reviewed by: Fatima Khursheed, Areeba Javed (design gate A14)  |  Status: draft (integration 2026-10-11: Use Cases v1.3, ADR-0001 to 0005; transitions T23, T25, T26 of the A3 table)&lt;br&gt;Realises: UC-B12, UC-D6, UC-I4; FR-B-14 to FR-B-17, FR-T-10, FR-T-11, FR-M-05; ADR-0004&lt;br&gt;Package: Borrowing lifecycle, Trust, reputation &amp; safety, Administration &amp; moderation (EscalationCase) (mapped to code packages in A8)&lt;br&gt;Rationale: Shows the dispute from the raising party's first action to the moderator's decision, including the no-response case and withdrawal. The booking moves to DISPUTED, then to COMPLETED through dispute_resolved (moderator) or back to its previous state through dispute_withdrawn. The resolved outcome goes to the Assurance Engine as evidence, which is the learning loop.&lt;br&gt;Notation (UML): stick figure = actor outside the system; box = object lifeline; white bar = activation; solid line + filled head = synchronous call; dashed line + open head = reply; solid line + open head = asynchronous message; dashed line + open head labelled «create» = create message; U-shaped arrow = self message; rounded box on a lifeline = state invariant; [text] = guard; alt / opt / ref = interaction frames. Replies that carry no data are omitted." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="2200" x="20" y="44" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
